# vehje, known gaps

## no-std

The top-level vehje bin crate currently runs on std. The bin entry
point uses `std::env::args` and `std::process::exit`, both of which
have no stable no_std equivalent on stable Rust without target-
specific entry-point work (a custom `#[start]` shim or a libc-backed
main wrapper). This is the canonical ecosystem-fit case for std per
the no_std-first doctrine in `PRINCIPLES.md`. A future round
explores whether a `core::ffi::CStr`-based argv reader and a
libc-backed exit wrapper can replace the std entry, at which point
this gap closes and `#![no_std]` lands. Tracked under follow-up.

## BufSink

`BufSink` is a fixed-buffer byte sink defined inside the crate's
`#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block, used only by the first-light emit test
to capture a target's output for assertion. It is not public surface
and never ships in the crate's compiled artifact, so it does not belong
in the DESIGN shipping contract. The `undocumented-type` lint flags it
because the tree-sitter surface extractor scans struct declarations
without excluding items gated behind `#[cfg(test)]`; documenting a test
fixture as public API would misrepresent the shipping surface, so the
honest resolution is this suppression rather than a DESIGN entry. The
proper fix is upstream in the lint (skip `#[cfg(test)]`-gated items),
tracked for a mockspace follow-up; until then this entry records why
the type is intentionally absent from the design docs.
